      "message": "\u003e\u003e Could we eventually/easily move to having the GrAtlasRenderTask use the path renderer chain...?\n\nThere\u0027s only one hiccup: GrPathRenderer uses GrSurfaceDrawContext, and GrSurfaceDrawContext can split its opsTask. Since GrAtlasRenderTask is itself one single opsTask, it needs to create its own ops and add them directly without an sdc. So basically, GrAtlasRenderTask would just need to create a DefaultPathOp internally and add it to the list. It shouldn\u0027t be hard.\n\nBut at the same time, how many devices don\u0027t support instanced rendering anymore?\n\n\u003e\u003e Is the MSAA check here necessary?\n\nDo you mean the MSAA check in onCanDrawPath? That one is not necessary. You\u0027re right. I just have it to preserve functionality during the refactor. I\u0027ll send out another CL that enables the atlas for kCoverage AA types shortly.",
